<title>FRANCE: French pension funds not seen operating until 1998.</title>
<headline>French pension funds not seen operating until 1998.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private pension funds will probably not begin to operate before 1998, a French parliamentary deputy said on Thursday, although legislation establishing their creation was approved by the National Assembly last month.</p>
<p>&quot;If we have truly got started by January 1, 1998, we'll have done good work,&quot; said Deputy Jean-Yves Chamard.</p>
<p>The National Assembly approved the bill on November 22, and the Senate is expected to take it up on December 12, with a second reading expected in January or February.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be a lot of regulatory details to work out requiring consultations,&quot; Chamard said.</p>
</text>
